      "stem": "Which fraction is equivalent to $\\frac{2}{3}$?",
      "options": [
        { "id": "a", "text": "$\\frac{4}{9}$" },
        { "id": "b", "text": "$\\frac{6}{12}$" },
        { "id": "c", "text": "$\\frac{10}{15}$" },
        { "id": "d", "text": "$\\frac{8}{15}$" }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "c",
      "explanation": "$\\frac{10}{15} = \\frac{10 \\div 5}{15 \\div 5} = \\frac{2}{3}$. You can also check by cross-multiplying: $2 \\times 15 = 30$ and $3 \\times 10 = 30$."
